<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="72525" href="schedule/2021/fall/CHLH/594/72525.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2021" href="schedule/2021.xml">2021</calendarYear><term id="120218" href="schedule/2021/fall.xml">Fall 2021</term><subject id="CHLH" href="schedule/2021/fall/CHLH.xml">Community Health</subject><course id="594" href="schedule/2021/fall/CHLH/594.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>HE </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Health Economics</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Health Economics:  Health policies and market forces impact the U.S. health care system in terms of access, cost, and quality. This course provides the perspective that economic reasoning is a valuable critical thinking approach to social science inquiry and demonstrates how this perspective helps students understand health care policy and market issues.  This course describes the role and methods of economics as applied to health care delivery in the United States.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Health Administration major(s).</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2021-08-23Z</startDate><endDate>2021-12-08Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="S3 ">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>04:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>M      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>3005</roomNumber><buildingName>Huff Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Mamaril" firstName="C">Mamaril, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>